{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense","id":17048,"title":"Do the pure make sense?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-24T02:51:47-08:00","id":17048,"title":"Do the pure make sense?","content":"Ok me and my group have what we feel is a decent understanding of the rather confusing cosmology in werewolf. One thing we still can't figure out is how dire, rabid, and silver are still alive. From all the lore in the books we have read we see that dire does nothing of value, and as far as we can tell silver is still burning alive. So that leaves rabid the weakest and most cowardly as the only one actively doing anything. Since most of the forsaken hate rabid wouldn't it be easy for winter to just round everyone up the first time he interfered with the forsaken and kill him. Wouldn't taking out the pure and letting their followers do their job unmolested be the smart thing to do? Are we missing something or just thinking to much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T03:16:13-08:00","id":17052,"title":"","content":"Rabid Wolf and Silver Wolf are &quot;just&quot; powerful spirits, from what I know. Destroying them would only cause the Pure to look for another Tribe Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T06:14:58-08:00","id":17098,"title":"","content":"I'd like to be annoying and say the title is misleading. <br /> <br /> But this how I look upon it. <br /> <br /> For the first thing, the Firstborn are not there to do the Urathas jobs for them. The werewolves killed Father Wolf and the werewolves must uphold those duties, not the Firstborn. While the Forsaken have gained the aid of the Firstborn they have not made the Firstborn their servants. Thus the Firstborn will not go about doing the Urathas jobs for them but will aid the Uratha when the Uratha follow their duties. If anyone will kill Rabid Wolf it will be the Uratha who will have to do it.<br /> <br /> Secondly I don't think that the Firstborn per necessity think in terms of maximal output for minimal effort, long term strategic planning and all that. They are more instinct and wolf-like in their actions and reasoning. Thus I do see that Winter Wolf can and probably would kick Rabid Wolf's ass if they get to fight but he would most certainly not kill his young brother when Rabid Wolf surrendered. That's not how I see the Forsaken's Firstborn anyway. And since the Firstborn does not form a common pack anymore they have probably little real incentive to go around picking for fights with random wolves outside of their own packs and territories.<br /> <br /> Thirdly I think that you underestimate the benefit that Dire and Silver Wolf gives to their &quot;children&quot;. Last I checked both of them provided Gifts to each of the Pure Tribes for instance as well as feeding the Pure the hatred on which their culture thrives and is built upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T09:40:00-08:00","id":17153,"title":"","content":"&quot;Just&quot; powerful spirits are really hard to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:05:27-08:00","id":17161,"title":"","content":"Echoing Gurkhal's post here. What if they're <b>banned</b> from utterly destroying their siblings?<br /> <br /> <b>Jesuncolo: </b>Did you know that spirits of rank 6 and above generate their rank in essence... <i>per turn?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:27:45-08:00","id":17175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17052#post17052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rabid Wolf and Silver Wolf are &quot;just&quot; powerful spirits, from what I know. Destroying them would only cause the Pure to look for another Tribe Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>True I suppose. Actually thinking of it like that it would make interesting story if the pure try to make a strong spirit like a idigam their totem. If they got the one that likes to resurrect people from wolfsbane it could make them near invincible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:39:27-08:00","id":17182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17098#post17098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly I don't think that the Firstborn per necessity think in terms of maximal output for minimal effort, long term strategic planning and all that. They are more instinct and wolf-like in their actions and reasoning. </div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true now that I think about it. really in our games we always used the totems as something similar to the gods in clash of the titans. But according to one of the books if you do that your doing it wrong. So the confusion probably just comes down to not really understanding how the totems operate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:50:50-08:00","id":17284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17182#post17182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also true now that I think about it. really in our games we always used the totems as something similar to the gods in clash of the titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to unpack that for those that haven't seen the film?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:08:34-08:00","id":17329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17284#post17284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to unpack that for those that haven't seen the film?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you haven't don't worry you didn't miss anything. What I mean is that in the movie and greek mythology the gods vie for power and use mortals as chess pieces. And if things are not going their way they will not hesitate to interfere and do the job themselves. But looking at one of the sidebars in I forget which book it says coincidentally the firstborn are not like greek gods. They are just wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:24:04-08:00","id":17335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17329#post17329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you haven't don't worry you didn't miss anything. What I mean is that in the movie and greek mythology the gods vie for power and use mortals as chess pieces. And if things are not going their way they will not hesitate to interfere and do the job themselves. But looking at one of the sidebars in I forget which book it says coincidentally the firstborn are not like greek gods. They are just wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the &quot;Ways of the Gods&quot; sidebar in Lore of the Forsaken noting that spirits of godlike potency are not just humans writ large.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn are wolves, yes, but they're spirit-wolves, and powerful ones at that \u2014 even Gafflings can manage intelligence enough to outwit the average mortal, but the priorities of spirits at the level of Incarnae are complicated immensely by the social-metaphysical rules of engagement in whose context they exist. Dire Wolf might well be able to rip skyscrapers from their foundations and gut battleships with the swipe of a mighty paw, but doing so risks the ire of whatever beings had plans for those things \u2014 and that of every other god whose allegiance they could bring to bear \u2014 and when gods fight in mortal lands, it is seldom the gods who suffer the greatest losses \u2014 which risks greater repercussions from third parties.<br /> <br /> So they stick to proxy-wars for dominance, because they're wolves sponsoring werewolves, and they echo back about as much sentiment as they supply natively to those werewolves, because they're spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-24-2013, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T03:19:22-08:00","id":17636,"title":"","content":"The Firstborn don't generally interfere in hunts on a pack level. They also don't generally attack each other (at least that is what the Forsaken and the Pure know and believe).<br /> <br /> The point is, do your own darn job. The Firstborn won't do your work for you.<br /> <br /> There are always options to mess with these assumptions. I posted a story hook that kinda sorta does so in my 1001 story hooks thread. <br /> <br /> <i> 7) Black Wolf doesn't speak to her children any more. Since last friday, the Hunters in Darkness - all of them - have ceased to feel any sort of connection to their tribal totem. It's as if they were Ghost Wolves, metaphysically. This also means that it's harder for the former Hunters in Darkness to invoke gifts powered by their spiritual patron and to gain the support of her spirit allies.<br /> <br /> It's about time for someone to quest into the Shadow, track down the Black Wolf (good luck with that!) and ask her what the hell is going on.<br /> <br /> If she still exists. And if she's still on the side of the Forsaken.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T17:00:38-08:00","id":18030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17161#post17161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoing Gurkhal's post here. What if they're <b>banned</b> from utterly destroying their siblings?<br /> <br /> <b>Jesuncolo: </b>Did you know that spirits of rank 6 and above generate their rank in essence... <i>per turn?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't. But the &quot;just&quot; on the &quot;powerful spirit&quot; still rimains true. They ARE powerful spirits, indeed. I know the loss of such a powerful spirit would be tremendous for any Tribe, and that's exactly what I'd do if my tribal totem has been wiped out. Look for another spirit who cares about us and our cause. That's not necessarily easy, and<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Just&quot; powerful spirits are really hard to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T14:02:34-08:00","id":19341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=17636#post17636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> 7) Black Wolf doesn't speak to her children any more....</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah we are probably going to steal that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T06:06:54-08:00","id":24320,"title":"","content":"If Rabid Wolf is a &quot;cowardly&quot; Incarna, then he probably has tremendously powerful &quot;run away&quot; and possibly &quot;launch debilitating attacks from concealed position&quot; type Numina.<br /> <br /> Werewolves or other Firstborn wouldn't necessarily have an easy time with him.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know... do you really want to risk catching the god rabies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:14:03-08:00","id":24388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17048-do-the-pure-make-sense?p=24320#post24320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, you know... do you really want to risk catching the god rabies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the other Firstborn won't risk it, any character I had wouldn't be going within a mile of that....unless they were pretty damn nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}